Description: speech dictation client for GNOME Wayland
 LemonVox records speech on request and sends it to a separately running
 Lemonade or compatible server for transcription and text cleanup. It pastes
 the result at the current keyboard focus without sending Enter.
 .
 The server must provide transcription, chat completions and compatible model
 discovery. Local and remote HTTP/HTTPS endpoints are supported. No server or
 models are bundled.
 .
 Global shortcuts and the dictation indicator require the included GNOME Shell
 extension, compatible with GNOME 46 and 51. X11 is not supported.
